From 3221d803156425830596df230c99a8391373e867 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roger Luethi <luethi@osism.tech>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:03:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rabbitmq: set prefetch count without stream fanout

Every service template sets rabbit_qos_prefetch_count only inside the
om_enable_rabbitmq_stream_fanout block. With stream fanout disabled the
option is not rendered at all, and services fall back to the
oslo.messaging default of 0, which means an unlimited prefetch: one
consumer channel can take every ready message of a quorum queue, so
load is not spread across workers and in-flight messages pile up in a
single consumer. om_rabbitmq_qos_prefetch_count has no effect.

The prefetch count is a consumer setting and applies to quorum and
classic queues alike, independent of how fanout is implemented. Render
it unconditionally, next to rabbit_quorum_queue.

Signed-off-by: Roger Luethi <luethi@osism.tech>
Upstream-Status: Pending
Bug: https://bugs.launchpad.net/kolla-ansible/+bug/2167251
